Package: tiltedTMLE
Title: Targeted Maximum Likelihood Estimation for Tilted Average Treatment Effects
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yixin", "Fang", email = "yixin.fang@abbvie.com", role = "aut"),
    person("Weili", "He", email = "weili.he@abbvie.com", role = "aut"),
    person("Ran", "Dai", email = "ran.dai@abbvie.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Implements targeted maximum likelihood estimators (TMLE) for a
    broad class of tilted average treatment effect (ATE) estimands, covering
    two related but distinct tilting-function settings. Fang, He, and Dai,
    "Targeted Learning for Externally Controlled Trials and Beyond"
    (AbbVie, 2026), treats the tilting function h(x) as a known, fixed
    weight prespecified by the user (e.g. h(x) = 1 for the ATE, or
    h(x) = the estimated propensity score itself for the ATT), estimated
    with a single targeting step. Fang, "Targeted Learning for Tilted
    Average Treatment Effects" (AbbVie, 2026), instead treats h(x) as a
    known function of an unknown nuisance function that must itself be
    estimated and iteratively targeted alongside the outcome regression:
    h(x) = eta(g(x)) for internally tilted estimands (ATE/ATT/ATC/ATO,
    tilting by a function of the treatment propensity score g(x) within a
    single study population), and h(x) = eta(s(x)) for externally tilted
    estimands (ATE-I/ATE-E/ATE-O, tilting by a function of the selection
    propensity score s(x) between an internal trial population and an
    external covariate-only population). All three settings share the same
    efficient-influence-function-based standard error construction.
